(Track B2 — mremap growth happy path. A >=4 MB regular file is written from a
 dynamic buffer of varied content, then read back into a fresh dynamic buffer.
 The read starts at the initial 4 KB capacity and grows across several mremap
 remaps to ~4.5 MB, so a broken no-copy growth path corrupts data or loses
 bytes, and full buffer equality plus a matching length proves every byte
 survived. Manual fallback of the mmap path is hard to trigger automatically:
 run under ulimit -v 8192 so mremap returns ENOMEM and the mmap plus rep movsb
 plus munmap fallback runs; the assertions must still hold.)

a buffer called chunk.
Append "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz_+" to chunk.

a buffer called big.
a number called i is 1.
While i is less than or equal to 70000,
  Append chunk to big,
  Increment i.

a number called wantlen is big's size.

open a file for writing called f at "/tmp/b320_mremap_fixture.bin".
Write big to f.
Close f.

open a file for reading called src at "/tmp/b320_mremap_fixture.bin".
a buffer called readbuf.
Read from src into readbuf.
Close src.
Delete the file "/tmp/b320_mremap_fixture.bin".

If readbuf is big then,
  If readbuf's size is equal to wantlen then,
    print "mremap grow ok".
  Otherwise,
    print "BUG: length wrong".
Otherwise,
  print "BUG: data mismatch".